# Security & Performance Best Practices

## Security Guidelines

### Authentication & Authorization
- Use Firebase Auth for all authentication flows
- Implement proper route guards and middleware
- Verify Firebase ID tokens for sensitive operations
- Use Firestore security rules to enforce data access
- Never trust client-side data validation alone

### Data Protection
- Sanitize user inputs to prevent XSS attacks
- Use HTTPS for all communications
- Store sensitive data server-side only
- Implement rate limiting for API endpoints
- Use Firebase App Check for additional protection (future)

### Privacy Considerations
- Users can only access their own profile data
- Room members can only see messages in their rooms
- Implement proper data deletion for user privacy
- Handle image uploads with proper access controls

## Performance Optimization

### Database Performance
- Use composite indexes for complex queries
- Implement pagination for message lists (20-50 messages per page)
- Use Firestore offline persistence for better UX
- Batch related operations to reduce read/write costs
- Clean up unused listeners and subscriptions

### Real-time Performance
- Use Realtime Database for ephemeral data (presence, typing)
- Implement proper onDisconnect cleanup
- Throttle typing indicators to avoid excessive updates
- Use efficient data structures for real-time features

### Frontend Performance
- Use React 19 concurrent features for better UX
- Implement proper loading states and skeletons
- Use Next.js Image component for optimized images
- Implement virtual scrolling for long message lists
- Use proper caching strategies

### Image Handling
- Compress images before upload (max 2MB)
- Generate thumbnails for image messages
- Use appropriate image formats (WebP when supported)
- Implement lazy loading for image galleries
- Cache images appropriately

## Monitoring & Error Handling
- Implement comprehensive error boundaries
- Log errors appropriately (avoid logging sensitive data)
- Use proper error messages for user feedback
- Monitor Firebase usage and costs
- Implement proper retry logic for failed operations

## Scalability Considerations
- Design for horizontal scaling from the start
- Use efficient data models to minimize reads/writes
- Implement proper connection pooling
- Consider CDN for static assets
- Plan for Firebase quotas and limits